w: From Heaven a- bove to earth I come, To bear good news to ev- ery home;
w: To you, this night, is born a Child Of Ma- ry, cho- sen mo- ther mild;
w: 'Tis Christ our God, Who far on high Had heard your sad and bit- ter cry;
w: He brings those bless- ings long a- go Pre- pared by God for all be- low;
w: These are the to- kens ye shall mark, The swadd- ling clothes and man- ger dark;
w: Now let us all, with glad- some cheer, Fol- low the she- pherds, and draw near
w: Wel- come to earth, Thou no- ble Guest, Through Whom e'en wick- ed men are blest!
w: Were earth a thou- sand times as fair, Be- set with gold and je- wels rare,
w: For vel- vets soft and sil- ken stuff Thou hast but hay and straw so rough,
w: Thus hath it pleased Thee to make plain The truth to us, poor fools and vain,
w: Ah, dea- rest Je- sus, ho- ly Child, Make Thee a bed, soft, un- de- filed,
w: Glo- ry to God in hi- ghest Heav'n, Who un- to man His Son hath giv-
