w: Glad ti- dings of great joy I bring, Where- of I now will say * and sing.
w: This ten- der Child of low- ly birth, Shall be the joy of all * your earth.
w: Him- self will your Sal- va- tion be, Him- self from sin will make * you free.
w: That in His heaven- ly king- dom blest You may with us for- ev- * er rest.
w: There shall ye find the young Child laid, By Whom the heav'ns and earth * were made.
w: To see this won- drous Gift of God, Who hath His own dear Son * bes- towed.
w: Thou com'st to share our mi- se- ry, What can we ren- der, Lord, * to Thee!
w: She yet were far too poor to be A nar- row crad- le, Lord, * for Thee.
w: Whe- reon Thou King, so rich and great, As 'twere Thy heav'n, art throned * in state.
w: That this world's ho- nor, wealth and might Are naught and wor- thless in * Thy sight.
w: Here in my poor heart's in- most shrine, That I may ev- er- more * be Thine.
w: en, While an- gels sing, with pious mirth, A glad New Year to all * the earth.
